  "limitations": [
    "The fake loopback endpoint establishes native mechanics, not real subscription validity or provider policy.",
    "Codex finalquota and unknownquota characterize distinct native phases; these tests do not establish a Swarm eligibility decision.",
    "Codex auth callback was triggered by an unauthorized WebSocket reconnect handshake; an in-band 401 is not equivalent.",
    "Codex callbacks are broadcast to initialized clients. The tested native TUI ignored this method during the observed 1.5-second interval; other clients are not proven safe.",
    "Claude empty SDK input also wakes completed work; it is not a safety discriminator or ordinary TUI continuation API.",
    "Claude 429 retry retained A after the credential file changed to B; 401 retry adopted B. A file replacement is not instantaneous request adoption.",
    "Real-grant canaries, integrated handover and continuation, human decisions, background actors, daemon gaps and ambiguous submission still require qualification."
  ],
